9	 * <em>hard</em> duplicate (whole {@code identityKey} match) has already been rejected with
10	 * 409 — and before {@link SaveOwner}, so the flags are computed against the owners that
11	 * existed before this create and are persisted with the new owner.
12	 *
13	 * <p>An owner is a possible duplicate when it shares an existing owner's {@code lastName}
14	 * (compared case-insensitively) and {@code postcode} while carrying a <em>different</em>
15	 * telephone. When such an existing owner is found, {@code possibleDuplicate} is set true
16	 * and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} to that owner's id (the lowest id when several match);
17	 * otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is false and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} null. A null
18	 * postcode never matches, so it is never a possible duplicate.
